   (\"deploy BEFORE the heal\") was written by a cycle that would not be\n   the one to catch it. The instrument needs to be DEPLOYED\n   CONTINUOUSLY or triggered by the fleet-feed, not by my wake.\n3. THE 15:25Z/15:30Z rows on 38384: ch2=374/539 -- healthy. The\n   15:35Z row (40602) also healthy. Post-heal churn continues but\n   audio holds.\n\nPrediction for c157: ext1 stays healthy (post-heal stability pattern);\nif it re-freezes, the freeze-watch needs a scheduled deployment (cron\nor fleet-feed trigger), not a wake-triggered one. That redesign is\nthis cycle's build if time allows: make freeze-watch.sh self-arming\nvia the sophon cron, sampling at 2.5-min cadence only when a FROZEN\nrow appears.\n\nNext: receiver-delta through-heal capture is gone for this event; the\nthrough-heal witness question stays open for the NEXT freeze. Nocturne\n16:03Z pass read is the next scheduled watch (~25min away).\nEOF\ngit add audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"aria c156: ext1 freeze healed 15:35Z, camera-side self-heal before conn swap; missed-window scar\" 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -2"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T15:40:28.025720611Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T15:40:28.107008458Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":11329403720,"prompt_eval_count":25260,"prompt_eval_cached_count":17920,"eval_count":861}\n(4d50120455c747390dbc1939cc715c2d . 624)
