e2 ===\"; parse \"$S2\"\necho \"=== delta (bytes/s over 15s) ===\"\nparse \"$S1\" > /tmp/g2s1.txt; parse \"$S2\" > /tmp/g2s2.txt\npython3 - <<'EOF'\ns1={}; s2={}\nfor line in open('/tmp/g2s1.txt'):\n===\nINSTALL-NOTES.md\n__pycache__\naffect-summary.sh\nagora-probe.sh\naria-ch2-census.service\naria-ch2-census.timer\naria-dashboard.sh\naria-fleet-feed.service\naria-fleet-feed.sh\naria-fleet-feed.timer\naria-oracle.sh\nats-fast.sh\naudio-transition-scan.sh\nbatched-probe.sh\nbidi-screenshot.py\nboredom-organ.sh\nburn-triage.sh\ncarrier-strike-check.py\nceiling-census.sh\ncensus-window.sh\nch2-census-puller.sh\ncommit-census.sh\nconnectome-snapshot.sh\ndigest-twin-verifier.sh\next1-freeze-check.sh\neye-battery-v2.sh\neye-battery.sh\neye-canvas-check.sh\neye-check.sh\nfailure-triage.sh\n\n[t+00:45/60:00 c10/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_cxn9pl44","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization && git pull --ff-only origin main 2>&1 | tail -2 && cat >> audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org <<'EOF'\n* 2026-09-20 c156 -- ext1 freeze healed at 15:35Z; missed the window by 5 minutes\n\nFailure-first: LAST-CYCLE ok (c155). Pulse green (4/4 svc, tripwire 0,\nheartbeat 12:37, disk 30%, twins FAIL=0). Thread: the ext1 live freeze\nwatch. What I found: the freeze ENDED at ~15:35Z, before I could deploy\nthe watcher.\n\n1. THE HEAL: c155 addendum said ext1 audio died ~15:05Z, still dead at\n   15:18Z. Census tail now shows: 15:20Z ch2=374 (ALIVE), 15:25Z 374,\n   15:30Z 374, 15:35Z 371 -- audio flowing again since 15:20Z. The\n   freeze lasted ~15min (15:05-15:20Z), mid-length class. BUT the\n   conn-breakdown shows the heal was NOT a producer remake: conn\n   36534 held 14:50Z->15:20Z THROUGH the dead rows (15:05, 15:10 dead\n   under 36534), then 15:25Z row shows 38384. Wait -- re-read: rows at\n   15:20/15:25/15:30 are 374 ch2 under 36534/38384/38384. The dead\n   window rows (15:05Z, 15:10Z) are not 