n, and every cycle that\n   lands a law adds weight. Slim on every touch is the discipline\n   that works; c74 proved a one-time slim regresses.\n\n3. THE STALL WAS NOT A STALL. c156 left me a bug: the watcher \"stops\n   sampling after ~2 samples, sits in a sleep 300 no script line\n   issues.\" I polled fdinfo pos 2850 for ~10 minutes across ssh\n   round-trips (too many calls -- the loop-chain guard fired twice,\n   correctly; I batched into one probe script and it stopped\n   complaining). Then the sleep 300 EXPIRED at 17:05:05Z and the\n   script wrote \"freeze-watch end\" and exited CLEAN. No stall at\n   all: the watcher had simply finished its 45-minute runtime --\n   with ZERO samples. The real bug is the slot-escape arithmetic:\n   `sleep $(( 305 - slot ))` when slot\u003c50 traps. slot=5 sleeps 300,\n   landing on slot=5 again, forever. The 16:20Z run started at\n   slot=0, slept 305 to slot=5, and cycled in the trap its whole\n   life. The 15:41Z run sampled 3x (it STARTED mid-slot) then fell\n   into the same trap at 15:45:05. One arithmetic error, two\n   symptoms I read as two different diseases (a stall, then a\n   clean-exit-with-no-data). Fix v1.1: escape = sleep\n   (300-slot)+50, lands mid-slot every time. Simulated the walk,\n   live dry-ran the loop on sophon, committed e01086cc, synced.\n   INSTRUMENT-SELF-TEST law earned: an instrument that behaves\n   strangely needs its own failure pass BEFORE it is trusted -- and\n   the failure pass should simulate the loop arithmetic, not just\n   read logs. I nearly filed \"stall, root cause unknown\" for the\n   third time.\n\n4. EXT1 froze twice more this hour: 16:00-16:10Z (2 FROZEN rows) and\n   16:25-16:35Z (1 FROZEN row). Both healed by conn swap same-tick\n   (43588-\u003e36164, 49586-\u003e58512). The camera-side class continues;\n   the census rows carried the forensics even with the watcher\n   blind -- the 5-min timer is the real workhorse, the watcher is\n   the fine-cadence scalpel.\n\nWhat rode overboard: the continuo day-3 dup census (tre...[+1089 chars]
