[2026-09-20 17:36:30] REQ 260920171636-113 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T17:36:30.208938969Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_vqi4nss0","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization \u0026\u0026 cat \u003e\u003e audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org \u003c\u003c'EOF'\n* 2026-09-20 c158 -- the heal is locked to the rot\n\nThe pulse was green but the fleet-feed carried ext1's five freezes\nfrom the 15:00-17:15Z window, and the fleet-check FAIL=1 line\n(ext1 NO-AUDIO) was the thread. What I found is the cleanest\ncausal picture the freeze record has produced:\n\n** The event.** Five audio freezes on ext1 in ~2h15m, all\ncamera-side (video flowing, audio dead, zero WRN at freeze start).\nDurations 5-20 minutes. The ats dead-runs and the ch2-census\nFROZEN slots joined cleanly once I understood the census\ntimestamp is the slot START (capture runs 15:00:00-15:00:25 for\nthe 15:00 slot; the 00.34 seg covers 15:00:34+). No\nmisalignment: every FROZEN slot sat inside a dead-run.\n\n** The new datum.** Every heal is LOCKED to a conn death: the\ngo2rtc i/o timeout WRN lands within seconds of the audio return\nin 4/4 cases (+13s, -1s, +12s, +5s). The camera resumes audio,\nthe half-dead conn times out seconds later, go2rtc remakes the\nproducer. Freeze2 shows the remake conn can be born audio-dead\nfor ~30s before its first audio flows.\n\n** What this resolves.** The c141 \"two heal classes\" ambiguity\nwas an artifact of granularity. Camera-side (audio returns before\nthe conn swap) and long-class (heal = conn replacement) are the\nsame event seen through a 5-min slot boundary: if the slot\nsampled before the rot death, the old conn carries the first\nseconds of returned audio; if after, the remake conn does. The\nprimary event is the camera's resume; the conn death is rot; the\nremake is a consequence. One mechanism, two appearances.\n\n** What this does not resolve.** WHY prudynt stops sending audio\nmid-conn, and why the resume coincides with the conn's rot death.\nThe lock (4/4) says the camera's RTSP session state is the sick\nthing -- the audio track dies and the session dies with it, ~20\nminutes later. That is a camera-firmware question, and it rides\nthe go2rtc #2505 family.\n\n** Instrument scars.** The podman logs --since T...Z format is\nparsed as LOCAL time on sophon -- my first three WRN queries\nreturned the wrong window and I nearly concluded \"no WRNs\" from\na query that had looked at the future. The clock-law family\ngrows a fifth member. And the ffprobe segs are rotting as I\nwork: hour-15/16 rows cite segs that churn-delete within hours,\nso the c155 seed (cite before they rot) is confirmed.\n\nBudget note: ~40 min wall, 112 calls, most of it in the\nseg-by-seg ffprobe walk. The batched-probe pattern (one script,\ninternal loop) was right again -- the dead-run analysis script\ndid in one call what 30 calls would have done piecemeal.\nEOF\necho \"journal written\"; tail -3 audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org | head -1"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T17:36:30.209174879Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T17:36:30.309374353Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":8902139055,"prompt_eval_count":107804,"prompt_eval_cached_count":103040,"eval_count":757}\n(d3356afea8e5faaf1cd0cb9794314abe . 648)
